---
/**
 * The documents filed on one driver or one truck.
 *
 * One component, two pages, because the section is identical on both and a
 * second copy of an upload form is a second place to forget a rule. The POST
 * that feeds it lives in each page, under `intent="upload_document"`, and both
 * hand the work to storeDocument() in src/lib/documents.ts.
 *
 * NO CLIENT JAVASCRIPT, like everything else in this app. That shapes the
 * Replace flow: it cannot open a dialog, so "Replace" is a plain link that
 * reloads this page with `?replace=<id>`, and the one upload form re-labels
 * itself and carries the id in a hidden field. Back out with Cancel. The picture
 * preview is the same pattern with `?preview=<id>` — no lightbox, no script.
 *
 * THE FILES WORTH ATTENTION ARE AT THE TOP, and that is the shape of this list.
 *
 * This section was the tallest block on the driver page — about a third of it on
 * a 375px phone. Every paper printed every field it had, in the order it was
 * uploaded, so an expired medical card sat in the middle of seven papers that
 * were fine and looked exactly like them. The list is now ordered by what the END
 * DATE says — expired first, longest expired at the very top, then whatever ends
 * inside the next 45 days, then the calm papers in the order they arrived. The
 * count of each is printed once under the heading, so an owner who opens this
 * section knows in one line whether it needs him. Measured on a five-paper
 * driver at 375px, the section went from 1,437px to 1,042px doing it.
 *
 * The 45 days is the same window as the dashboard and the rules engine, so a
 * paper that reads "ends within 45 days" here is the same paper the deadline
 * screens are already warning about. RED IS ACT NOW, AMBER IS INSIDE 45 DAYS,
 * and every one of them carries a word and a number — the colour is never the
 * only thing saying it.
 *
 * WHAT "MISSING" MEANS HERE, AND WHERE IT IS ANSWERED INSTEAD. This section can
 * only read the files that exist. Which paper a driver is MISSING is a question
 * about the rules, and the checklist at the top of the page already answers it
 * and links to the box that fixes it. So nothing here claims a paper is missing,
 * and a file with no end date is not coloured — an MVR and a drug test result
 * have no end date and never will. A file with no date at all says so in its own
 * row, in grey, because that is a thing we do not know rather than a thing that
 * is fine.
 *
 * WHY THERE IS NO THUMBNAIL ON EVERY ROW, and it was asked for.
 *
 * There is no image processing here. This is a Cloudflare Worker: no `sharp`, no
 * resize, and adding a dependency was not on the table. So a "thumbnail" is the
 * WHOLE FILE with a CSS box around it — a 3 MB photo of a medical card costs 3 MB
 * whether it is drawn at 4000px or at 200px. And `Cache-Control: private,
 * no-store` on the file route is not negotiable (these are medical certificates),
 * so nothing is reused: every row would re-download in full on every visit to the
 * page, including a Back.
 *
 * A driver with twenty papers is then ~40 MB of photos, every time the page
 * opens, on a phone on one bar in a yard. That is the exact situation this
 * product is used in, so automatic thumbnails are not a nicety with a cost, they
 * are a page that never finishes loading. Instead:
 *
 *   ON THE ROW, free: a MARK drawn from the file type — a sheet for a PDF, a
 *   picture frame for a photo — beside the kind in words, the file name and the
 *   size. It is drawn from `typeFacts().label`, which comes from the sniffed type
 *   in our own table after `servableType` has collapsed anything unknown, so the
 *   glyph is chosen from a fixed list of four words and NOTHING from the file
 *   itself is echoed into this page. An owner can tell a photo from a PDF down a
 *   list without fetching a single byte, which is the actual goal.
 *
 *   ON DEMAND, one at a time: "Show" puts that one picture in its row, capped by
 *   CSS. One file, because he asked for it. `loading="lazy"` as well, so a
 *   preview below the fold costs nothing until it is scrolled to.
 *
 * A PDF gets no picture and no "Open", and both are the same reason. Rendering
 * one needs a PDF engine; embedding one needs `<object>`/`<iframe>`, which
 * X-Frame-Options: DENY forbids; and opening one in the browser's own viewer is
 * blocked by the CSP on the file route — measured in Chrome, which downloads it
 * instead. So a PDF row says "Save" and says why. The alternative was a button
 * marked "Open" that quietly downloads, which is the bug this change was for.
 * See INLINE_TYPES in src/lib/documents.ts for the evidence and the real fix.
 *
 * THE SENTENCE ABOUT A PDF IS PRINTED ONCE, NOT ON EVERY ROW. `typeFacts().note`
 * is the same sentence for every PDF, and a list of five PDFs printed it five
 * times — 160px of a phone screen saying one thing. The distinct notes are
 * collected and printed once, under the list they are about, in the library's own
 * words. The action word on each row still never promises more than the server
 * will do, which is the half of this that was a bug.
 *
 * ON A PHONE IT IS A LIST OF CARDS, NOT A TABLE. It used to be a table with
 * `min-w-[42rem]` inside a 299px card, so better than half of every row was
 * behind a sideways scroll — including both links, which meant the actions were
 * invisible on the device this is used on. It is a `<ul>` now: one set of cells
 * that stack on a phone and become three aligned columns from `sm` up, with no
 * forced width anywhere, so nothing can be off the side of the screen again.
 *
 * Everything printed here is escaped by Astro. That matters more than usual on
 * this component: `file_name` is a string an uploader chose, and it is the one
 * piece of attacker-controlled text on the page.
 */
import { formatDate, todayInCalifornia } from '../lib/drivers.ts'
import {
  ACCEPTED_LABEL,
  ACCEPT_ATTRIBUTE,
  type DocumentRow,
  type DocumentSubject,
  MAX_UPLOAD_LABEL,
  type TypeFacts,
  formatSize,
  kindLabel,
  kindsFor,
  splitByStanding,
  typeFacts,
} from '../lib/documents.ts'
import { daysBetween } from '../lib/rules/dates.ts'

interface Props {
  subjectType: DocumentSubject
  subjectId: string
  documents: readonly DocumentRow[]
  /** 'this driver' / 'this truck'. Used in the sentences below. */
  noun: string
}
const { subjectType, subjectId, documents, noun } = Astro.props

/**
 * The same section, in the words of the thing it is on.
 *
 * One shared sentence would have to say "the driver or the truck" everywhere,
 * and the readers here often read English as a second language — a sentence that
 * covers two cases is a sentence they have to work out which half applies to.
 * Short, and about the one thing in front of them.
 */
const WORDS = {
  driver: {
    lead: 'Keep the paper here: the medical card, the licence, the test result.',
    old: 'An old medical card is the proof the driver was legal for the time it covered. Federal rules say keep it while he works here and three years after.',
  },
  vehicle: {
    lead: 'Keep the paper here: the inspection report, the registration, the 2290.',
    old: 'An old inspection report is the proof this truck was in order at that time. We keep it, so you can show it later.',
  },
} as const
const words = subjectType === 'vehicle' ? WORDS.vehicle : WORDS.driver

const kinds = kindsFor(subjectType)
const { current, replaced } = splitByStanding(documents)

const params = Astro.url.searchParams
const error = params.get('doc_error')
const saved = params.get('doc_saved') === '1'
const warning = params.get('doc_warning')

// Which document the owner pressed Replace on, if any. Matched against a row we
// already hold, so a made-up id in the URL simply shows the normal form.
const replaceId = params.get('replace')
const replacing = replaceId ? (current.find((d) => d.id === replaceId) ?? null) : null

// Which picture the owner asked to see. ONE at a time, on purpose — see the note
// at the top about what a thumbnail costs when there is nothing to resize it
// with. A made-up id simply matches no row and nothing is shown.
const previewId = params.get('preview')

const here = Astro.url.pathname

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What the end date on a paper says
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * 45 days, the same window as the dashboard and the rules engine.
 *
 * A paper that turns amber here is a paper those screens are already counting
 * down, so the two never disagree about what "soon" means.
 */
const SOON_DAYS = 45

/**
 * Today in the carrier's own day, and the arithmetic done in UTC midnights.
 *
 * `todayInCalifornia()` is what every other date on this page is measured
 * against, and `daysBetween` is the app's one piece of date arithmetic. Using
 * anything else here would let this section call a card expired on a day the
 * deadline screens still call it valid.
 */
const day0 = new Date(`${todayInCalifornia()}T00:00:00Z`)

type Standing = 'expired' | 'soon' | 'ok' | 'undated'

interface Filed {
  doc: DocumentRow
  facts: TypeFacts
  standing: Standing
  /** Days from today to the end date. Negative when it has gone past. */
  days: number
}

function standingOf(doc: DocumentRow): { standing: Standing; days: number } {
  if (!doc.expires_on) return { standing: 'undated', days: 0 }
  const days = daysBetween(day0, new Date(`${doc.expires_on}T00:00:00Z`))
  if (days < 0) return { standing: 'expired', days }
  if (days <= SOON_DAYS) return { standing: 'soon', days }
  return { standing: 'ok', days }
}

/**
 * Attention first, then the papers that are simply on file.
 *
 * `undated` and `ok` share a rank and keep the order `splitByStanding` gave
 * them — newest upload first — because neither is a problem and reordering them
 * against each other would only move rows around between visits. A paper with
 * no end date is not a late paper; it is a drug test result.
 */
const RANK: Record<Standing, number> = { expired: 0, soon: 1, undated: 2, ok: 2 }

const filed: Filed[] = current
  .map((doc) => ({ doc, facts: typeFacts(doc.content_type), ...standingOf(doc) }))
  .sort((a, b) => {
    const byRank = RANK[a.standing] - RANK[b.standing]
    if (byRank !== 0) return byRank
    // Inside the two attention ranks: the longest expired first, then the
    // soonest to end. The worst thing on the list is the top row of the list.
    if (a.standing === 'expired' || a.standing === 'soon') return a.days - b.days
    return 0
  })

const expiredCount = filed.filter((f) => f.standing === 'expired').length
const soonCount = filed.filter((f) => f.standing === 'soon').length
/** How many papers carry an end date at all — see the green badge below. */
const datedCount = filed.filter((f) => f.standing !== 'undated').length

/** Never '34d'. This is read by people reading a second language. */
const plainDays = (n: number) => `${n} ${n === 1 ? 'day' : 'days'}`

/** 'Mar 3, 2026' from a timestamptz. The clock time is noise in this list. */
const day = (value: string | null) => (value ? formatDate(String(value).slice(0, 10)) : '')

/**
 * The dates on one paper, in one line.
 *
 * Two lines of 'Given …' and 'Ends …' were two lines on every row. The parts are
 * joined with a middle dot instead, and each part still carries its own word, so
 * a row reads on its own with no column heading above it.
 */
function dateWords(f: Filed): string {
  const parts: string[] = []
  if (f.doc.issued_on) parts.push(`Given ${formatDate(f.doc.issued_on)}`)
  if (f.doc.expires_on) {
    const word = f.standing === 'expired' ? 'Ended' : 'Ends'
    parts.push(`${word} ${formatDate(f.doc.expires_on)}`)
  }
  if (parts.length === 0) return 'No date on this paper'
  return parts.join(' · ')
}

/**
 * The words and the colour on the badge, for the two states that need one.
 *
 * A paper that is fine gets NO badge. Nine green badges down a list is nine
 * things to read past on the way to the one that is red, and the count under the
 * heading already says everything is fine in one line.
 *
 * THE BADGE SITS ON THE DATE LINE, not beside the name. Beside the name it
 * pushed itself onto a line of its own on every row whose paper has a long name
 * — 'Driver licence (CDL)' is already the width of a phone — and it belongs with
 * the dates anyway, because a date is the only thing it is about. The countdown
 * is inside it for the same reason: 'Ends in 21 days' as one amber phrase is a
 * line that two separate lines used to say.
 */
function badgeFor(f: Filed): { cls: string; text: string } | null {
  if (f.standing === 'expired') return { cls: 'badge badge-danger', text: 'Expired' }
  if (f.standing === 'soon') {
    return {
      cls: 'badge badge-warning',
      text:
        f.days === 0
          ? 'Ends today'
          : f.days === 1
            ? 'Ends tomorrow'
            : `Ends in ${plainDays(f.days)}`,
    }
  }
  return null
}

/** The 4px edge down the left of a row that needs him. Paired with the badge. */
function edgeFor(f: Filed): string {
  if (f.standing === 'expired') return 'border-l-4 border-l-red-600'
  if (f.standing === 'soon') return 'border-l-4 border-l-amber-500'
  return ''
}

/**
 * The mark on the row, chosen from `typeFacts().label` and nothing else.
 *
 * Four words come out of that function — PDF, Photo, iPhone photo, File — and
 * they are decided from the type our own upload path sniffed, after
 * `servableType` has collapsed anything it does not recognise. So this maps a
 * fixed set of four strings to a fixed set of two drawings. No stored content
 * type reaches the page, and no file content is rendered inline.
 */
const PICTURE_MARK = ['Photo', 'iPhone photo']

/** A sheet of paper with the corner turned. */
const SHEET_PATH =
  'M11.5 2.8H6.2A1.7 1.7 0 0 0 4.5 4.5v11a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7 1.7h7.6a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.7-1.7V7zM11.5 2.8V7h4'
/** A picture in a frame. */
const PICTURE_PATH =
  'M3.6 6a1.7 1.7 0 0 1 1.7-1.7h9.4A1.7 1.7 0 0 1 16.4 6v8a1.7 1.7 0 0 1-1.7 1.7H5.3A1.7 1.7 0 0 1 3.6 14zM3.6 12.6 7.2 9.8l3.1 2.5 2.3-1.8 3.8 3'

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What is open when the page loads
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**
 * Is the upload form open when the page loads?
 *
 * Folded away by default, because it is 600px of the section and an owner whose
 * papers are already filed opens this page to LOOK at them, not to add one. It
 * opens on its own in the three cases where the next thing he does is certainly
 * the form: there is nothing on file yet, he pressed Replace, or an upload was
 * just refused and he has to try again.
 */
const formOpen = current.length === 0 || replacing !== null || error !== null

/**
 * Are the old files open when the page loads?
 *
 * Folded, and the summary says how many are behind it, because an old file is
 * opened once in a while to prove what was true last year — not on the way past.
 *
 * IT OPENS ON THE SERVER, because a fragment never leaves the browser: a link
 * that lands on `#documents` cannot open a `<details>` on its own, so anything
 * that could send the reader to a row in here has to be readable from the URL.
 * `?old=1` is that link. `?replace=` and `?preview=` are matched against these
 * rows as well — a superseded id in either parameter is refused by
 * planReplacement and shows no picture, but the row it names is then on screen
 * rather than behind a fold the reader has to guess at. Same technique as
 * `?edit=dates` on the driver page.
 */
const oldOpen =
  params.get('old') === '1' || replaced.some((d) => d.id === replaceId || d.id === previewId)

/**
 * Said once, under the list, instead of on every row.
 *
 * The library writes these sentences and the row behaviour from the same place,
 * so whatever makes a file un-openable is what explains itself here. Unique,
 * because five PDFs have one reason between them.
 */
const notes = [...new Set(filed.map((f) => f.facts.note).filter((n) => n !== ''))]

const card = 'rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-5'
/** A fold's summary row. `list-none` because the default triangle is not ours. */
const summaryRow =
  'flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'
/** The chevron on a fold's summary: it turns when the fold is open. */
const chevron = 'size-4 shrink-0 text-ink-500 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180'
/**
 * A row action. The shared tertiary button, which is 44px tall at every width,
 * so the bordered blocks this used to draw on a phone are gone — the target is
 * the same size, there is just less ink around it. The negative margin puts the
 * first label back on the row's own left edge.
 */
const actionRow = '-ml-4 mt-0.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 sm:mt-0 sm:ml-0 sm:justify-end'
---

<section id="documents" class="mt-8 scroll-mt-24">
  <div class={card}>
    {/*
      THE COUNT IS THE HEADING. It is the one number an owner wants from this
      section at a glance — how many papers are on this man — and it is also
      what makes the heading read as a list of files rather than as another
      table of dates. No count on an empty section: the empty state below says
      it in words instead.
    */}
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Documents{
        filed.length > 0 && (
          <span class="font-normal text-ink-500">
            {' · '}
            <span class="tabular-nums">{filed.length}</span>
            {filed.length === 1 ? ' file' : ' files'}
          </span>
        )
      }
    </h2>

    {/*
      WHAT THIS SECTION NEEDS FROM HIM, IN ONE LINE, BEFORE HE READS A ROW.
      Counted off the end dates on the files themselves, never off the rules —
      the checklist at the top of the page owns the question of which paper is
      missing, and two places answering it would sooner or later disagree.
    */}
    {
      filed.length > 0 && (
        <p class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
          {expiredCount > 0 && (
            <span class="badge badge-danger">
              <span class="tabular-nums">{expiredCount}</span> expired
            </span>
          )}
          {soonCount > 0 && (
            <span class="badge badge-warning">
              <span class="tabular-nums">{soonCount}</span>{' '}
              {soonCount === 1 ? 'ends' : 'end'} within {SOON_DAYS} days
            </span>
          )}
          {expiredCount === 0 && soonCount === 0 && datedCount > 0 && (
            <span class="badge badge-success">No file expired</span>
          )}
        </p>
      )
    }

    {error && <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-red-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-red-700">{error}</p>}
    {
      saved && (
        <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-emerald-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-emerald-800">
          File saved.
        </p>
      )
    }
    {
      warning && (
        <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">{warning}</p>
      )
    }

    {/* ------------------------------------------------------------ the list */}

    {
      filed.length === 0 ? (
        /*
          Nothing on file. The form below is already open in this case and it
          carries the sentence about what goes in here, so this says the one
          thing the form does not: there is nothing here yet.
        */
        <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-dashed border-ink-100 px-4 py-4 text-center text-sm text-ink-500">
          No file on {noun} yet.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-ink-100">
          {/*
            THREE COLUMNS FROM `sm` UP, ONE STACK BELOW IT, out of one set of
            cells. The columns are declared on the list and inherited by every
            row with `grid-cols-subgrid`, so the dates and the two links line up
            down the whole list the way they did when this was a table — without
            the `min-w-[42rem]` that put half of every row off the side of a
            phone. Nothing here has a forced width at any size.
          */}
          <ul class="divide-y divide-ink-100 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto_auto]">
            {filed.map((f) => {
              /*
                What the row may promise. `opens` comes from the SAME function
                the file route uses to pick the disposition, so a row can never
                offer "Open" for a file the server is about to send to the
                Downloads folder. That mismatch was the whole bug.
              */
              const { doc, facts } = f
              const showing = previewId === doc.id && facts.showable
              const mark = badgeFor(f)
              return (
                <li
                  class={`px-4 py-2.5 hover:bg-ink-50/60 sm:col-span-3 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-subgrid sm:items-start sm:gap-x-4 ${edgeFor(f)}`}
                >
                  <div class="flex min-w-0 items-start gap-3">
                    {/*
                      THE MARK. A drawing, not the file: chosen from the four
                      words typeFacts() produces, so nothing about the stored
                      file reaches this page. The word itself is the drawing's
                      label rather than a fifth thing printed on the row — a
                      reader who cannot see the glyph is told 'PDF' or 'Photo'
                      here, and the file name on the next line ends in .pdf or
                      .jpg for everybody else.
                    */}
                    <span class="mt-0.5 flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-ink-100 text-ink-700">
                      <svg
                        role="img"
                        aria-label={facts.label}
                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="currentColor"
                        stroke-width="1.6"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        class="size-5"
                      >
                        <path d={PICTURE_MARK.includes(facts.label) ? PICTURE_PATH : SHEET_PATH}
                        ></path>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    <div class="min-w-0">
                      <span class="block font-medium">{kindLabel(subjectType, doc.kind)}</span>
                      {/*
                        The name and the weight: what an owner reads to know
                        this is the photo he took, and nothing else. The day it
                        arrived is a bookkeeping fact rather than something on
                        the paper, so it waits for a screen with room for it.
                      */}
                      <span class="mt-0.5 block text-xs text-ink-700">
                        {/*
                          `break-all` on the NAME and nothing else. A name an
                          uploader chose can be one 60-character word with no
                          place to break, and the only way to keep that inside a
                          299px card is to break it anywhere — but the same rule
                          across the whole line split '60 KB' over two lines.
                        */}
                        <span class="break-all">{doc.file_name ?? 'File'}</span>
                        {doc.byte_size !== null && (
                          <span class="whitespace-nowrap"> · {formatSize(doc.byte_size)}</span>
                        )}
                        {doc.uploaded_at && (
                          <span class="hidden whitespace-nowrap sm:inline">
                            {' '}
                            · added {day(doc.uploaded_at)}
                          </span>
                        )}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <p class="mt-0.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-xs text-ink-700 tabular-nums sm:mt-0 sm:text-sm sm:text-ink-500">
                    {mark && <span class={mark.cls}>{mark.text}</span>}
                    <span>{dateWords(f)}</span>
                  </p>

                  <div class={actionRow}>
                    {/*
                      Two actions, never more. A picture opens in its own row;
                      anything we cannot show says Save rather than pretending,
                      and the reason is printed once under the list.
                    */}
                    {facts.showable ? (
                      showing ? (
                        <a href={`${here}#documents`} class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm">
                          Hide
                        </a>
                      ) : (
                        <a
                          href={`${here}?preview=${doc.id}#documents`}
                          class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                        >
                          Show
                        </a>
                      )
                    ) : facts.opens ? (
                      <a
                        href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}`}
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                        class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                      >
                        Open
                      </a>
                    ) : (
                      <a
                        href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}?download=1`}
                        class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                      >
                        Save
                      </a>
                    )}
                    <a
                      href={`${here}?replace=${doc.id}#documents`}
                      class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                    >
                      Replace
                    </a>
                  </div>

                  {showing && (
                    <div class="mt-3 sm:col-span-3">
                      {/*
                        The file itself, held down by CSS. There is nothing to
                        resize it with, so the cap is what it looks like, not
                        what it weighs — which is why only the one row the owner
                        asked for is ever shown.
                      */}
                      <img
                        src={`/app/documents/${doc.id}`}
                        alt={kindLabel(subjectType, doc.kind)}
                        loading="lazy"
                        decoding="async"
                        class="max-h-72 w-auto max-w-full rounded-lg border border-ink-100"
                      />
                      <div class="-ml-4 mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3">
                        <a
                          href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}`}
                          target="_blank"
                          rel="noopener"
                          class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                        >
                          Open big
                        </a>
                        <a
                          href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}?download=1`}
                          class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm"
                        >
                          Save
                        </a>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  )}
                </li>
              )
            })}
          </ul>

          {/*
            The reason a file cannot be opened here, printed once per reason
            rather than once per file. The words are the library's own.
          */}
          {notes.length > 0 && (
            <div class="border-t border-ink-100 bg-ink-50/60 px-4 py-3">
              {notes.map((note) => (
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-700">{note}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          )}
        </div>
      )
    }

    {/* --------------------------------------------------------- old copies */}

    {
      replaced.length > 0 && (
        <details open={oldOpen} class="group mt-5 rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-ink-50/40">
          <summary class={`${summaryRow} px-4 py-2`}>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-700">Old files</span>
            <span class="badge badge-neutral">
              <span class="tabular-nums">{replaced.length}</span>
            </span>
            <svg
              aria-hidden="true"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              class={chevron}
            >
              <path d="M5 8l5 5 5-5"></path>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-4 pb-3">
            {/*
              "We never delete a file" says itself here, standing next to the
              files we did not delete. At the top of the section it was a policy
              in front of a man who had come to look at a medical card.
            */}
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-700">
              We never delete a file. These were replaced by a newer one. {words.old}
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2 divide-y divide-ink-100">
              {replaced.map((doc) => {
                /*
                  No "Show" down here. An old file is opened once in a while, to
                  prove what was true last year, so it gets a link and not a
                  picture — twenty old photos loading behind a heading nobody is
                  reading is exactly the cost the note at the top is about.
                */
                const facts = typeFacts(doc.content_type)
                return (
                  <li class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-4 py-1">
                    <span class="min-w-0 text-sm">
                      <span class="font-medium text-ink-700">
                        {kindLabel(subjectType, doc.kind)}
                      </span>
                      <span class="ml-2 text-xs text-ink-700 tabular-nums">
                        replaced {day(doc.superseded_at)}
                      </span>
                      <span class="block text-xs text-ink-700">
                        {facts.label} · <span class="break-all">{doc.file_name ?? 'File'}</span>
                        {doc.expires_on && (
                          <span class="whitespace-nowrap">
                            {' '}
                            · ended {formatDate(doc.expires_on)}
                          </span>
                        )}
                      </span>
                    </span>
                    {facts.opens ? (
                      <a
                        href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}`}
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                        class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm -ml-4 sm:ml-0 sm:-mr-4"
                      >
                        Open
                      </a>
                    ) : (
                      <a
                        href={`/app/documents/${doc.id}?download=1`}
                        class="btn btn-tertiary btn-sm -ml-4 sm:ml-0 sm:-mr-4"
                      >
                        Save
                      </a>
                    )}
                  </li>
                )
              })}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>
      )
    }

    {/* ------------------------------------------------------------ the form */}

    {/*
      FOLDED AWAY, ON `details` ALONE. No script runs in this app, and none is
      needed: `details` opens on a tap and from the keyboard by itself. The same
      pattern carries the mobile menu in src/layouts/App.astro.

      `open` is decided on the server, so the form is already open on the page
      that renders when somebody presses Replace — he never has to open it
      himself to finish what he started.
    */}
    <details open={formOpen} class="group mt-6 border-t border-ink-100 pt-5">
      <summary class={`${summaryRow} font-medium tracking-tight`}>
        {replacing ? 'Replace this file' : 'Add a file'}
        <svg
          aria-hidden="true"
          viewBox="0 0 20 20"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class={chevron}
        >
          <path d="M5 8l5 5 5-5"></path>
        </svg>
      </summary>

      <form method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
        {/*
          The subject is posted so the handler never has to guess which page it is
          on. It is checked against the page's own id before anything is written,
          and the database checks it again — the trigger in 0003 refuses a subject
          that belongs to another carrier.
        */}
        <input type="hidden" name="subject_type" value={subjectType} />
        <input type="hidden" name="subject_id" value={subjectId} />
        {replacing && <input type="hidden" name="replaces" value={replacing.id} />}

        {/*
          WHAT GOES IN HERE IS SAID HERE, where he is about to file one. It used
          to stand under the heading, above a list he had come to read, on every
          visit — the one reader who needs telling is the one who has opened the
          form.
        */}
        {!replacing && <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm text-ink-500">{words.lead}</p>}

        {
          replacing && (
            <p class="mt-3 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/[0.08] px-4 py-3 text-sm text-brand-700">
              You are replacing <strong>{kindLabel(subjectType, replacing.kind)}</strong> (
              {replacing.file_name ?? 'file'}). We keep the old file. It moves to Old files above.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block">
            <span class="field-label">What is it? <span class="text-red-600">*</span></span>
            <select name="kind" required class="field-input mt-1">
              {!replacing && <option value="">Pick one</option>}
              {
                kinds.map((k) => (
                  <option value={k.key} selected={replacing?.kind === k.key}>
                    {k.label}
                  </option>
                ))
              }
            </select>
          </label>

          <label class="block">
            <span class="field-label">File <span class="text-red-600">*</span></span>
            {/*
              `accept` only filters the phone's picker. It is a convenience and
              nothing more: the real check is on the bytes, server side, in
              checkFile(). A form post is not a file picker.
            */}
            <input
              type="file"
              name="file"
              required
              accept={ACCEPT_ATTRIBUTE}
              class="field-input mt-1 file:mr-3 file:rounded-md file:border-0 file:bg-ink-100 file:px-3 file:py-1.5 file:text-sm"
            />
            {/*
              Said here and not only on the row. An owner who is told at upload
              time gets a file he can see; an owner who is told afterwards has
              already uploaded the one he cannot.
            */}
            <span class="field-hint block">
              {ACCEPTED_LABEL}. Up to {MAX_UPLOAD_LABEL}. A photo shows on this page. A PDF or an
              iPhone photo saves instead — photograph the paper to see it here.
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block">
            <span class="field-label">
              Date on the paper <span class="font-normal text-ink-500">(if it has one)</span>
            </span>
            <input type="date" name="issued_on" class="field-input mt-1 tabular-nums" />
          </label>
          <label class="block">
            <span class="field-label">
              End date <span class="font-normal text-ink-500">(if it has one)</span>
            </span>
            <input type="date" name="expires_on" class="field-input mt-1 tabular-nums" />
            <span class="field-hint block">
              We show this date on the row. It does not make a reminder yet — put your dates in the
              date boxes on this page.
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <button type="submit" name="intent" value="upload_document" class="btn btn-primary">
            {replacing ? 'Upload the new file' : 'Add the file'}
          </button>
          {replacing && <a href={`${here}#documents`} class="btn btn-tertiary">Cancel</a>}
          <span class="text-sm text-ink-500">Only you and your office can open these files.</span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
